{"id":"kelp-rseth-2026","slug":"kelp-rseth-2026","sub":null,"name":"Kelp-related rsETH holder Safe exploit 2026-09-15 (Uniswap v4 module): Yoink uses the attacker's prepared executor","date":"2026-09-15","one_liner":"One block after the attacker's prepare() tx, Yoink called the attacker's own executor and pulled 2,900 rsETH from a holder's Safe, paying a 18.93 ETH builder tip; 2,882.37 rsETH went back to a Safe signer about 30 hours later.","bot":"Yoink","race_type":"deploy-window-copy","narrative":"Attacker deployed executor 0x10605ee4 (block 25980523 idx 155) and called prepare() 0xd28cebb8 (tx 0x0a7d69ab, block 25980524 idx 207). Yoink tx 0x0e7680b0 (block 25980525 idx 0, one block later) called the executor's function 0x882d6bfa(2900e18,0,0) via its gen3 contract and received 2,899.99999 rsETH pulled out of the victim Safe's Aave position. A read-only eth_call of that same function from an arbitrary address reverts 'not prepared' at the state after block 25980523 and succeeds at the state after 25980524: the call only became possible once prepare() was mined. A second, unrelated searcher (0x492d2552, tx 0x16b9ddf9, idx 3) called the same executor function in the same block and its internal call reverted (already drained). In round 3 the same attacker did deploy (869) -> prepare (870) -> execute at idx 0 of the next block (871); in round 1 its finishing tx (nonce 4) never landed and the nonce was later burned by a self-transfer (blk 25980578). Yoink was therefore pre-empting the attacker's next-block finishing step.","chain":"ethereum","verdict":"confirmed-onchain","t0_ms":1789447127000,"pre_merge":false,"premerge_note":null,"slot":15218592,"block":{"number":25980525,"hash":"0xfc5eccff33da2beaea4a26cb8bd14d9c3d63cc02f9a79af1f9e782643eaca742","ts_ms":1789447127000,"ntx":27,"builder":"builder.ultrasound.money","fee_recipient":"0x6c42a0b5d13059fa36d5567ab04f83bab57bbf0e","gas_used":6520111,"base_fee_gwei":0.063989473,"raw":{"block":"raw/rpc/block_25980525.json","rec